From c68f235e4a0e6018668a44226b727e54068ab9d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: git: support unconditional raw ref updates

Raw ref updates need guarded and unconditional modes. Existing bookmark,
tag, and Gerrit pushes must keep their lease checks

Represent the safety policy explicitly. Use force-with-lease for guarded
updates and a forced refspec for unconditional updates

Record Git's up-to-date result separately. This lets higher layers
validate a caller-provided lease even when Git skips an update that
already has the requested target

Refs #4388

